Voice Agent Bridge — Copyright © 2026 Pintjes. All rights reserved.

END USER LICENSE AGREEMENT (EULA)

1. Purpose

This agreement is made between you, the user ("you"), and Pintjes ("the
author"). It governs the use of Voice Agent Bridge, including its files, its
documentation and its updates ("the Software"). By installing or using the
Software, you accept this agreement. If you do not accept it, do not install or
use the Software.

2. Ownership

The Software is the property of the author and is protected by copyright. It is
licensed to you, not sold. No ownership right in the Software is transferred to
you. All rights not expressly granted to you are reserved.

3. License granted

The author grants you a personal, non-exclusive and non-transferable right to
use the Software for your own needs, on the Home Assistant installations you
manage. The Software may be subject to a trial period or to a license key; the
applicable conditions are then given to you when you obtain the Software or the
key.

4. Restrictions

Unless the author gives written permission, you may not:
a) copy the Software, except to install it and to make backup copies;
b) distribute, publish, lend, rent, sell, sublicense or otherwise make the
   Software available to third parties;
c) modify or adapt it, create derivative works from it or reuse any part of it
   in other software;
d) decompile or disassemble it, or extract its source code by reverse
   engineering;
e) circumvent, disable or tamper with a protection or license measure;
f) remove or change the copyright and ownership notices.

These restrictions do not limit the rights that mandatory law gives to the
lawful user of a software (for example backup copies, observing how it works or
interoperability), nor the rights that the license of a third-party component
gives you (article 6).

Bug reports, suggestions and ideas you send to the author may be used by the
author freely and without compensation.

5. Your data

The data of your installation (your devices, your configuration, your
conversations) remains yours. The Software runs on your installation and
sends nothing to the author. However, to produce its answers, it sends to
Claude, Anthropic's service, through Claude Code and your own subscription or
API key: the text of your requests (spoken or written), the conversation
history, your notes about the house, and the context of your home that the
agent reads to answer (for example the states, history, logs and configuration
of your devices). Anthropic processes this data under its terms and privacy
policy, not under this agreement. By using the Software, you consent to this
transmission.

6. Third-party components

The Software uses or contains third-party components, which remain under their
own license. This agreement does not change those licenses and does not limit
the rights they give you. Components, in the versions shipped with this version
of the Software:
- Claude Code 2.1.322 — proprietary software of Anthropic PBC, subject to
  Anthropic's terms (Commercial Terms of Service). It is not included in the
  Software's repository: it is downloaded from Anthropic's website when the
  image is built on your installation. Your use of Claude Code and Claude, and
  its cost, depend on your agreement with Anthropic;
- ha-mcp 9.2.0 — MIT. Installed as is, unmodified, with its Python
  dependencies (separate packages installed by pip when the image is built,
  each under its own license, mainly MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, ISC and, for
  certifi, MPL-2.0);
- the base image of the Software: Python 3.13 (PSF license) on Debian
  (licenses of its packages, including curl, bash and ca-certificates).
The Software's code uses only the Python standard library; the web panel loads
no third-party library. The copyright notices and the texts of these licenses
are in the installed packages.

7. Warning specific to the use

The Software lets an artificial intelligence agent answer your voice or written
requests and act on your home. The agent's answers and actions are provided
without any guarantee of accuracy: the agent may be wrong, misunderstand a
request or act in an unexpected way, and it may control your devices. You
remain solely responsible for them. The Software must not be used as a means of
safety of people or property, as an alarm or as an access control, nor for any
function whose failure could cause personal injury or property damage. The use
of Claude remains subject to Anthropic's terms and to your subscription.

8. No warranty

To the fullest extent permitted by law, the Software is provided "as is",
without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose, and error-free or uninterrupted operation.
The rights that mandatory law gives you, in particular as a consumer, are not
affected.

9. Limitation of liability

To the fullest extent permitted by law, the author is not liable for indirect
or non-material damages, nor for loss of data, profits or business, nor for
damage to your devices or your home, nor for charges billed by Anthropic,
whether resulting from the use of or the inability to use the Software. The
author's total liability is limited to the amount you paid for the license of
the Software. Nothing in this agreement excludes or limits the author's
liability for willful misconduct, death or personal injury, nor in cases where
the law forbids it.

10. Term and termination

This agreement lasts as long as you comply with its terms. It ends
automatically, without formality, if you do not comply with them. You may end it
at any time by uninstalling the Software and destroying your copies. When the
agreement ends, you stop using the Software. Articles 2, 4, 7, 8, 9 and 12
remain applicable.

11. Earlier versions

The versions of the Software published before version 1.1.3 were published
under the GPL-3.0-or-later license: they remain governed by that license. This
agreement governs version 1.1.3 and the following ones.

12. Governing law and courts

This agreement is governed by Belgian law. The Belgian courts have jurisdiction
over any dispute, subject to the mandatory jurisdiction rules applicable to
consumers.

13. Miscellaneous

This agreement is the entire agreement between you and the author regarding the
Software. If a clause is held void or unenforceable, the other clauses remain in
force. Failing to enforce a right is not a waiver of that right.

"Claude", "Anthropic", "Home Assistant", "Assist" and the other trademarks named
belong to their owners; the Software is an independent project, not affiliated
with them.
